2.4 Create Voucher
 In order to create Vouchers, user must select from the available active
VID.
 Vouchers can be created using Manual Entry or Excel Upload Option
provided in Voucher Posting Module.
 Only one voucher batch can be created against one VID.
 In case a Voucher batch is rejected, then user can reuse the VID to
create new vouchers.
2.4.1 Manual Entry
 The screen to allow user to create voucher posting.
SBI Project Solution Document for CR No: 26040135 Version 1.3
TCS SBI Confidential Page 10
 Remarks – screen to allow user to input either a common remark for
the entire batch or separate remarks against each voucher entry.
Remarks will be alpha-numeric only.
 Branch – Branch code entered by the user, will be searched in the
database and only available branch can be selected for voucher
posting. This is a mandatory field.
 Currency – User must choose currency from the dropdown. This is a
mandatory field.
 CGL - CGL code entered by the user, will be searched in the database
and only available CGL can be selected for voucher posting. This is a
mandatory field.
 Amount - This is a mandatory field. The maximum allowed value is
9999999999999999.9999. No negative value is allowed.
 Type – User must select either Debit or Credit for every voucher entry.
 Product Code – This is an optional field; user can add numeric product
code up to 8 digits.
 Add row – allows user to add the voucher row.
 Delete row– Will delete the voucher row.
 Schedule execution time –The user can choose immediate execution
of voucher posting or set a preferred voucher execution time by
setting a specific time. The scheduling is allowed for 30 mins onward
and till 23:59 of the day.
 Submit – All the voucher entries will be validated with as per business
validations. User can submit the voucher batch only if all the
validations are satisfied.
2.4.2 Excel upload
The Bulk upload screen will allow user to create bulk vouchers using the excel
template.
Excel Template
The screen to provide downloadable excel template which will have
 Predefined column order: Branch, Currency, CGL, Amount, Type,
Remarks, Product Code. A * mark will be displayed against mandatory
columns. The column order needs to be maintained as it is while
uploading. 



